    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Time-Bounded Dual Constraint Relaxation with Mandatory Compensatory Recovery Period: Temporarily raise both thresholds for a defined production window (not to exceed 5 consecutive working days): FatigueIndex ceiling raised to 0.65 and Noise ceiling raised to 85.0 dB. Both relaxations must be accompanied by mandatory compensatory measures: a minimum 48-hour reduced-load recovery period immediately following the surge window, continuous real-time physiological monitoring of all operators, and daily occupational health check-ins. This option enables full demand fulfillment with zero deadline gap but represents a formal deviation from established human-centric safety standards and requires sign-off from the occupational health officer and a union or worker-representative acknowledgement before activation.
