    5. noise_level / measurement basis
       Q: Is the 80 dB(A) limit a shift-long time-weighted average (TWA), meaning short loud bursts above 80 dB are permissible if the average stays compliant, or is it a never-exceed instantaneous ceiling that the optimizer must satisfy at every sampled moment?
       A: The limit is interpreted as an 8-hour equivalent TWA (Leq) per occupational exposure standards (e.g., ISO 9612); instantaneous peaks above 80 dB(A) are allowed provided the shift TWA remains at or below 80 dB(A).

